WHAT: Further increases speed-mode inliner aggressiveness. Raises multi-use
inlining limits and reduces multi_block_multi_use_penalty from 12 to 6.

WHY: Building on step 3's success, targeting governance functions that still
had uninlined helpers. The reduced penalty means multi-block functions used
from multiple call sites are more likely to be inlined.

GAS IMPACT: -414 gas total.
  governance/delegate: -138
  governance/propose: -138
  governance/vote: -138
  Other contracts: no change.

CODEGEN IMPACT: Only governance benefited. The delegate/propose/vote functions
have deeper call chains that the previous limits didn't reach.

TEAM NOTES: Diminishing returns from inliner tuning. Steps 3 and 4 together
saved ~876 gas, mostly on governance. Math, escrow, amm/swap, and merkle
didn't improve — their bottlenecks are elsewhere (ABI decode patterns, stack
scheduling, array init overhead). Further inliner tuning hits a ceiling
when the underlying IR patterns are inefficient.
